codex
A stricter review caught one important G4 issue before handoff: the first moment is a linear sum constraint that a solver can enforce essentially for free, so sampling arbitrary subsets would be an over-generous “noise” baseline. I’m tightening `random_candidate` to sample uniformly from distinct \(k\)-subsets already satisfying \(b_1\), changing `search_space` to \(\binom pk/p\), and re-running all gates against that stronger prior.
