\end{equation}
Then, the bounds of the  statement follows from the above equality and  from the fact that if $k \leq q-\sqrt{q}+1$,  $\frac{q-i}{\sqrt{q}+k-i-1}\geq \frac{q-j}{\sqrt{q}+k-j-1}$ holds for $0\leq j\leq i\leq k-1.$
