codex
I found a second audit-quality issue in G6: the fourth “by-hand” attack was secretly passed the planted orbit template, which a solver never sees. Even though it failed, that was not a faithful in-context probe. I’m replacing it with a moment-ratio additive-partition scan that derives every tested partition and balancing shift solely from the rendered `p`, `k`, and moments.
apply patch
